# PART 1: TECHNOLOGY ARCHITECTURE

Build a responsive, full-stack web application using:

- Frontend: React + TypeScript.
- UI: Tailwind CSS and reusable component architecture.
- Animation: Framer Motion.
- Charts: Recharts or equivalent interactive visualization library.
- Icons: Lucide React.
- Backend: Node.js server-side runtime.
- Database: Firebase Cloud Firestore.
- Authentication: Firebase Authentication with Google Sign-In and role-based access.
- File Storage: Firebase Storage.
- AI Integration: Google Gemini API through secure server-side endpoints.
- Mathematical Rendering: KaTeX or MathJax.
- Interactive Mathematics: SVG, Canvas and suitable mathematical visualization libraries.

Use modular architecture with reusable components, separate services, hooks, utilities, database models, and API layers.

Keep all Gemini API credentials and sensitive operations on the server. Never expose API keys in client-side code.

Use real Firestore persistence, not just local state or mock data.

Create appropriate Firebase security rules with strict role-based permissions and student-data isolation.

The application should support future integration with GitHub, Netlify or Cloud Run deployment workflows.

